      "id": 1,
      "text": "Stanwood was founded as Centerville in 1866 and renamed Stanwood in 1877 after postmaster Daniel O. Pearson.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanwood%2C_Washington",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town hosts the Pilchuck Glass School, founded 1971 by Dale Chihuly, making Stanwood a hub for glass art.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanwood%2C_Washington",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A short railroad, the Hall and Hall Railway, ran between the depot and downtown from 1904 to 1938, linking Stanwood to the main line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanwood%2C_Washington",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2022, Snow Goose Transit launched a minibus service that now serves Stanwood and parts of Camano Island.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanwood%2C_Washington",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Stanwood’s historic downtown and East Stanwood feature preserved early 20th‑century buildings, reflecting the town’s dual‑center layout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanwood%2C_Washington",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The city’s two National Register of Historic Places listings include the 1903 IOOF Public Hall, once used by fraternal groups before becoming a historical society museum.",
